Feature: holon

  The Prism measures itself, the owner included, and improves only its own
  tunable parameters, in the browser. After afflom/verdant-resonance's
  Teleology (the reflexive holon: every facet has a directive, an objective
  and a KPI floor; the whole and the co-observer are facets; self-reference
  alone is bounded; the observer reconciles the dissonance between the
  co-observer and the whole) and its conservatory curation (the 64-cell
  Rule-30 register, the defect = 0 gate, strict Pareto dominance, kappa-named
  claims, a non-regressing floor). Two proved guests decide: PrismHolon what
  the observer does next for one facet, PrismCurate whether one candidate
  replaces what runs.

  @HL-01 @build
  Scenario: The Prism's observer decides what to do next for each facet only as the proved PrismHolon answers: every facet, the owner and the Prism itself among them, has a directive, an objective and a KPI floor; nothing changes while halted, on the Prism's own measures alone, for a parameter no spec marks tunable, or when the owner and the Prism agree; high dissonance is reconciled toward the owner; and a floor the facet regressed below is restored
    Given the PrismHolon guest built from app/src/PrismHolon.lex.tex, refused unless its SHA-256 is the pinned one
    When every one of its 96 requests is decided
    Then each answer is the generated mirror's answer and keeps all nine guarantees
    And every facet in site/holon/table.mjs has a directive, an objective, a KPI and a floor
    And the Prism root routes "holon <request>" to PrismHolon::holonDispatch
    And Lean proves the nine guarantees with exactly the axioms Quot.sound and propext

  @HL-02 @build
  Scenario: A candidate set of a facet's tunable parameters replaces what runs only as the proved PrismCurate answers: a Rule-30 hypothesis only when it strictly Pareto-dominates what runs, a reconciliation only when it eases the owner's dismissals, never with a humane defect, without the owner's gestures, below the floor, off its spec's bounds or step, or while halted, and always under a kappa label the kappa facet admitted, minted once
    Given the PrismCurate guest built from app/src/PrismCurate.lex.tex, refused unless its SHA-256 is the pinned one
    When every one of its 2048 requests is decided
    Then each answer is the generated mirror's answer and keeps all thirteen guarantees
    And the Prism root routes "curate <request>" to PrismCurate::curateDispatch
    And Lean proves the thirteen guarantees with exactly the axioms Quot.sound and propext

  @HL-03 @build
  Scenario: The observer runs in the owner's browser on the resonance engine's signals: it measures every facet's KPI from the owner's own gestures, advances the 64-cell Rule-30 register (the spec's vectors), replays each candidate on the window, carries one line to each facet through the root guest, obeys no answer it does not expect, keeps its state (parameters, register, claim labels, no content) in this browser, and hands only adopted parameters to the engine
    Given a synthetic engine whose owner keeps only what is most salient, and the kappa guest
    When the observer sees rounds of the owner's gestures
    Then the Rule-30 register steps as the spec's vectors say
    And the parameters it adopts stay on their spec's bounds and step and ease the owner's dismissals with zero defects
    And every adoption is a sha256 kappa label in a bounded ledger, minted once
    And halted, too few of the owner's gestures, an unexpected answer or an unadmitted label change nothing
    And a regressed incumbent is restored to the floor, and the state survives a reload
